{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641943,"nonce":"eZd+IDuN7tF+lOYSg5Fx1lVGfJE=","title":"malloc trim gate calls mallinfo2 and compares free bytes, not releasable bytes","message":"tiered_backend.rs release_unused_pages (474738bd): mallinfo2 locks every arena and walks every free bin (O(free chunks)). The gate then trims when fordblks \u003e= 16 MB, but fordblks counts the top chunk, fastbins and fragmented free chunks that malloc_trim cannot return, so it measures free bytes, not releasable bytes.\n\nA process whose arenas keep over 16 MB of fragmented free chunks after a compile burst pays the mallinfo2 walk and the full malloc_trim on every Scratches::clear, release_if_unused and finished compile, more than the unconditional trim did. Below the threshold it still takes every arena lock and walks every free list; only the madvise pass is skipped.\n\nDirection: gate on a cheaper signal (bytes allocated by the compile burst, or a counter of compiled functions since the last trim) and measure on a fragmented heap.","files":null}]}